From 8f4a79a3bd9299aab2da96c9782bd0571c061829 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sjsj001 <>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:12:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Dial custom TCP connections off the network thread

CreateTransportClientSocket ran the custom dialer inline, and the dialer
returns only once TCP is connected. Every stream of the engine waited
out each new session's handshake with it on the network thread: a
black-holed proxy stalled them all for the dialer's timeout, and a burst
of new sessions dialed one after another.

The factory now returns a socket whose Connect runs the dialer on the
thread pool, under a ScopedBlockingCall, and adopts the descriptor into
a TCPClientSocket back on the network thread, which then does
everything else. A socket destroyed before its dial returns, or an
engine shut down, drops the reply, and the descriptor is closed with it.
A socket tag applied before Connect is applied once there is a
descriptor. A socket dials once: connect jobs make a new socket for
every attempt.

The connect timing is unchanged: connect_start was already taken before
the factory ran. The connect job's backup timer can now fire during a
slow dial and start a second one, as it does for system sockets. UDP
dials stay on the network thread: QUIC connects its socket
synchronously unless AsyncQuicSession is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
